},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/40/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 40\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":733,\"bb\":567963,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"एषा तेऽभिहिता सांख्ये बुद्धिर्योगे त्विमां श‍ृणु ।
बुद्ध्या युक्तो यया पार्थ कर्मबन्धं प्रहास्यसि ॥ ३९ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":734,\"bb\":661,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/b661/\",\"body_value\":\"eṣā te ’bhihitā sāṅkhye
buddhir yoge tv imāṁ śṛṇu
buddhyā yukto yayā pārtha
karma-bandhaṁ prahāsyasi\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":735,\"bb\":662,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/b662/\",\"shadow_value\":\"eṣā – all this; te – unto you; abhihitā – described; sāṅkhye – in analytical study; buddhiḥ – intelligence; yoge – in work without fruitive result; tu – but; imām – this; śṛṇu – just hear; buddhyā – by intelligence; yuktaḥ – dovetailed; yayā – by which; pārtha – O son of Pṛthā; karma-bandham – bondage of reaction; prahāsyasi – you can be released from.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"eṣā\",\"translation\":\"all this\"},{\"word\":\"te\",\"translation\":\"unto you\"},{\"word\":\"abhihitā\",\"translation\":\"described\"},{\"word\":\"sāṅkhye\",\"translation\":\"in analytical study\"},{\"word\":\"buddhiḥ\",\"translation\":\"intelligence\"},{\"word\":\"yoge\",\"translation\":\"in work without fruitive result\"},{\"word\":\"tu\",\"translation\":\"but\"},{\"word\":\"imām\",\"translation\":\"this\"},{\"word\":\"śṛṇu\",\"translation\":\"just hear\"},{\"word\":\"buddhyā\",\"translation\":\"by intelligence\"},{\"word\":\"yuktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"dovetailed\"},{\"word\":\"yayā\",\"translation\":\"by which\"},{\"word\":\"pārtha\",\"translation\":\"O son of Pṛthā\"},{\"word\":\"karma-bandham\",\"translation\":\"bondage of reaction\"},{\"word\":\"prahāsyasi\",\"translation\":\"you can be released from\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":736,\"bb\":663,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/b663/\",\"body_value\":\"Thus far I have described this knowledge to you through analytical study. Now listen as I explain it in terms of working without fruitive results. O son of Pṛthā, when you act in such knowledge you can free yourself from the bondage of works.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":737,\"bb\":664,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/b664/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":738,\"bb\":665,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/b665/\",\"body_value\":\"$26\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":739,\"bb\":666,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/b666/\",\"body_value\":\"$27\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":740,\"bb\":667,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/b667/\",\"body_value\":\"Of course, atheistic sāṅkhya-yoga has nothing to do with bhakti-yoga, yet the unintelligent claim that the atheistic sāṅkhya-yoga is referred to in the Bhagavad-gītā.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":741,\"bb\":668,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/2/39/b668/\",\"body_value\":\"One should therefore understand that buddhi-yoga means to work in Kṛṣṇa consciousness, in the full bliss and knowledge of devotional service. One who works for the satisfaction of the Lord only, however difficult such work may be, is working under the principles of buddhi-yoga and finds himself always in transcendental bliss. By such transcendental engagement, one achieves all transcendental understanding automatically, by the grace of the Lord, and thus his liberation is complete in itself, without his making extraneous endeavors to acquire knowledge. There is much difference between work in Kṛṣṇa consciousness and work for fruitive results, especially in the matter of sense gratification for achieving results in terms of family or material happiness. Buddhi-yoga is therefore the transcendental quality of the work that we perform.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 2.39\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 2.39\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2c:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next